Z||000000||87GT||06-12-2000||12:01 AM||||Hello all.  I need to ask a question about something my clutch did the other day.  I was driving along to get a pizza and everything is great.  I park the car, go get the pizza and come back to my car.  I get in and go and I noticed when I pulled out that the car almost stalled out which is unusual cause it never happened before, so I pulled back over to see what the heck was different.  It turns out my clutch is engaging and disengaging right at the floor instead of up high like it normally does.  This is the first bit of trouble it has give me since Ive owned it(14 mths.)  It shifts gears great and is very drivable it just disengages right at the floor and I dont like the feeling.  What could the problem be?  ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Shiner||06-12-2000||12:21 AM||||I would place my bet on clutch hydraulics (sp?)  This is a big problem on a good amount of Fieros.  Hopefully, it's just air in the line, and you need to bleed it out (oh, the joy!)  Check out the master cyl, slave cyl, and hydraulic lines for leaks.  Also check to make sure the slave cyl. is extending all the way, and that the bracket is in good condition.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Cooter||06-12-2000||12:34 AM||||If you have had the car that long and not done anything to the clutch hydraulics, consider yourself lucky! More than likely, you will soon have a component failure- either the master or slave cylinder. My advice would be go ahead and order rebuild kits for both. If you are not inclined to rebuild the old ones, new cylinders are available at an additional cost. More advice: If you want them within the next month, do not order them from carparts.com||||reg||1
Z||000003||87GT||06-12-2000||11:26 AM||||Thank you guys for giving me some info on this problem.  Ill probably get the rebuild kits that you mentioned cooter. thanks!||||reg||1
